        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">A primary bacterial infectious disease that results_in infection located_in skin, has_material_basis_in Treponema carateum, which is transmitted_by contact with skin and mucous membrane of an infected person. The infection has_symptom pruritic plaque, which slowly enlarges and becomes pigmented and hyperkeratotic.</owl:annotatedTarget>
